Does thinking about this in a mixture or stick-breaking framework help any?  re-parametrize theta_1,...,theta_N by group index, s_1,...,s_N and ``locations", theta^{*}_1,...,theta^{*}_N.  it somewhat de-couples updating the discrete assignments from moving the continuous locations.  Of course, the number of observations assigned to each continuous location will update in the sampler.

