Yes, B is just getting reassigned different indexes --- no nonlinear
transforms going on.

I'd highly recommend replacing

  flow ~ poisson (exp (mu));

with

  flow ~ poisson_log(mu);

because it'll be both faster and more arithmetically stable.

I'd also recommend not using tabs in code, but that's just a style
thing.

- Bob

> On Nov 7, 2014, at 9:34 AM, Linas Mockus <linasm...@gmail.com> wrote:
