> > Few notes about the model.  It is very similar to
> >   http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravity_model_of_trade#Econometric_Estimation_of_Gravity_Equations
> >
> > except that M_i and M_j have to be estimated.  Therefore we have much more parameters.
> > It looks like :
> > F_ij ~ Poisson (lambda_ij)
> > log(lambda_ij) <- A[i] + B[j] - beta * distance_ij + ...
> >
> > The physical meaning:
> >     exp(A[i]) is attractive potential of country i
> >     exp(B[j]) is repulsive potential of country j
> >     F_ij = A_i * B_j * exp (-beta * distance_ij + ...)
