I was lurking around on the Stan development mailing list when I came across the plans for WebStan <https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/stan-dev/emscripten/stan-dev/MaDPhUager0/CKRHEqQRoaoJ> post where the merits of compiling Stan models with emscripten were discussed. For those of you who doesn't know emscripten, it's a really cool project with the aims of making a compiler that takes, say, a c++ program (like a compiled Stan model) and compiles it down to javascript! If emscripten could compile Stan models we are inches from running Stan models in the browser :) So I've downloaded emscripten and tried to compile a simple Stan model but without any success (but I could have done all kinds of stupid mistakes). So my question(s):

Have anyone here tried compiling a Stan model using emscripten? Did it succeed? Is there some reason why it shouldn't work?

Was sort of hoping I could extend my javascript Gibbs sampling demo (http://www.sumsar.net/best_online/) with some Hamiltonian goodness...

