I'm encountering the same issue as Heiko. If you have a chain that takes a week
to run it's rather frustrating when the system has some unexpected security
upgrade and needs to reboot 6 days into the run. I also use a system where
there's a wallclock limit on jobs.

A strategy I've seen is to have "checkpoints" made every n (warmup) iterations
and allow resuming from the last checkpoint.

Thanks,

Allen

