You can get the solution for just one time point with a size-1
array.  No way to overload this to be a scalar, at least not yet.
We've been discussing how we want to overload the solver given its
rather large number of arguments.  (I know this would be easier if
Stan had named arguments like R rather than working like C++.)

I'll fix the bug Daniel found as soon as I can.  I'm traveling for
a week, so it's very unlikely I'll be able to fix it before the middle
of next week.

- Bob

