I guessed exceptions or I/O, so I was half right.

I don't see how we could disable Stan's exceptions without
a heroic refactoring effort.  But even more importantly, I don't
think we should disable exceptions.  I think it's the right way
to do what we're doing.  An alternative would be a C-style hack
that, say, wrote to some designated location and then used a goto
to jump, but I don't think that's possible out of context, and I
don't want to have to start passing return codes and making returns
reference arguments and all the other ugliness that was error handling
in plain C.

- Bob

