They have the same effect on parameters, but will have
different log densities by a constant because of the truncation.
That constant isn't necessary in expressing a model in Stan
because we only need the log density up to an additive constant.

They won't be the same if the truncation point on sigma is
not a constant or if the parameters to the cauchy are not constant.

- Bob

