Allen:

I was just curious why you wanted the full posterior.
I'm asking because I'd like an example at hand where
it made a difference in this kind of model.

Heiko and Allen:

That's a good point about restarting just due to robustness
issues, but as I believe I said in some other thread, that
requires a bit more work if we wind up needing to save during
warmup because there's dynamic state with the mass matrix
estimates which work online using Welford's algorithm.

Janne:

When Andrew says everything here, he means everything.  We have
as high priority to-do items:

  * Laplace approximations to variance using (penalized) MLE.

  * max marginal likelihood (MML), with similar variance estimates
    for hierarchical models along the lines of lme4 (but with different
    algorithms that we are hoping will generlize beyond hierarchical
    glms.

  * stopping and restarting (at least during sampling --- warmup's
    a bit trickier and may not get done right away)

- Bob

