Yes, state of the algorithm is well defined.  We'd just
need to dump out the accumulators used by Welford's algorithm.

CmdStan streams out samples to a file.  RStan and PyStan
save them in memory by default (I'm not even sure if they're
configurable to stream to a file, but if not, they should probably
have that option).  MatlabStan and Stan.js just wrap CmdStan.

